<section class="need"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Why it matters</h2>
<p class="sub">Iron deficiency and the emotional strain of pregnancy are common, serious, and often overlooked.</p>
<ul class="facts">
<li><span class="fact-n">1 in 4</span><p>pregnant women in the Philippines had anaemia in 2023.<a class="ref" href="about.html#src2" aria-label="Source 2">[2]</a></p></li>
<li><span class="fact-n">1 in 5</span><p>new mothers in low- and lower-middle-income countries experience a common mental disorder, such as depression or anxiety, after childbirth.<a class="ref" href="about.html#src5" aria-label="Source 5">[5]</a></p></li>
</ul>
<p class="sub after-list">The World Health Organization recommends daily iron and folic acid for every pregnant woman.<a class="ref" href="about.html#src4" aria-label="Source 4">[4]</a> <a href="about.html#sources">See all sources</a></p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<h2>What one kit holds</h2>
<p class="sub">Every mother in a cycle receives the same complete kit during her prenatal care.</p>
<!-- [PLACEHOLDER: photo of one real kit, or a scan of a handwritten card shared with the student's permission. Ask the founders; never use stock images.] -->
<div class="kit">
<div class="kit-card"><h3>A handwritten card</h3><p>Written by a student volunteer in the U.S. with a word of encouragement and a verse or prayer for each mother.</p></div>
<div class="kit-rest">
<div><h3>Iron (ferrous) tablets</h3><p>Bought locally by the clinic's staff with funds we send. Iron supports the normal growth and development of her baby and helps her feel less tired.</p></div>
<div><h3>Two health guides</h3><p>One on taking ferrous tablets, one on mental health in pregnancy and new motherhood. Written in Tagalog and English and checked by the clinic's medical team before printing.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div></section>

<section class="mission"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Our mission</h2>
<p>Heartlines International nurtures the health, hope, and future of underserved mothers and children around the world &mdash; meeting real community needs through health, education, and mental-health support, so that every mother and child knows they are seen and valued.</p>
</div></section>

